---
title: Ham and havarti focaccia sandwich
servings: 1
yield: 1 sandwich
tags: [pork, make-ahead]
source: Ham and Cheesy by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/ham-and-cheesy
---

> The focaccia fills an 18-inch sheet tray and the mustard mayonnaise makes
> about a kilogram: a restaurant batch for one sandwich. Start the dough a day
> ahead.

== Focaccia ==

Whisk the @active dry yeast{7%g} into the @water{850%g} ~{1%minute}, until
dissolved. Mix in the @extra virgin olive oil{25%g} and @honey{20%g}.

Add the @00 flour{1.1%kg} and mix by hand into a shaggy dough. Add the
@kosher salt{40%g} and knead ~{3%minutes}, until smooth and elastic. Cover and
refrigerate ~{24%hours}.

Oil an 18-inch #sheet tray{} generously with @extra virgin olive oil{30%g}.
Press the cold dough out toward the edges until it springs back, then leave it
~{2%hours} at room temperature, until it fills the tray.

Heat the oven to 450°F and bake ~{20%minutes}, until golden. Cool on a
#wire rack{}.

== Mustard mayonnaise ==

Pulse the @roasted garlic{75%g}(chopped) and @scallions{75%g}(chopped) to a
paste in a #food processor{}.

Add the @dijon mustard{75%g}, @whole grain mustard{30%g} and
@black pepper{1%tbsp}(ground) and pulse to combine. Add the
@mayonnaise{650%g} and process smooth. Refrigerate.

== Sandwich ==

Toss the @mixed greens{1%cup} with the @ponzu{1%tbsp} and a pinch of
@kosher salt{}.

Split a piece of focaccia and spread both cut sides with the mustard
mayonnaise. Layer the @Black Forest ham{5%oz}, @havarti{1.5%oz} and the
greens on the bottom half.

Close, cut in half, and serve.
